{
  "about": "v1.61.0: Talk to OBS's wire contract, read by both test suites (src-tauri/src/obs/; src/data/obs.test.ts) and by e2e/tauri-mock.ts. Production code never imports it, and the fake OBS server (src-tauri/src/obs/fake.rs) never reads it. hostSamples: what parse_host makes of a typed address (ip, the canonical address in use, or error, a HostError whose message is in hostErrors) and whether the page's hostPrecheck passes it on to Rust. gateTable: a Hello's d and what the version gate makes of it (pass, tooOld, badVersion, or notObs: not a Hello). textKindTable and readsFromFileTable: which inputs are text sources, and when one reads a file. followTable: what follow_op does with an output event (event: stream, a StreamStateChanged, or record, a RecordStateChanged; outputState as OBS sends it) for a count-up that follows the stream or the recording (setElapsed: SetElapsed {ms: the time since the event was read, running: true}; pause, resume: TimerOp::Pause, TimerOp::Resume; seed: GetStreamStatus or GetRecordStatus, then join_seed; null: nothing). seedTable: what join_seed does with a GetStreamStatus or GetRecordStatus answer and the timer's phase (timerNow: only whether it is running counts). failureTable: what request_failure makes of an error code for each kind of work, in failureResults' words: a success, a timeout and a 207 after ExitStarted (which ends the connection retrying/obsExiting) are the driver's, not in it. obsStatusSamples: ObsStatus values as Rust serializes them, every state and every reason. authVectors: Identify's authentication from a password and Hello's salt and challenge (Python hashlib and Node crypto agree on each).",
